sequenceDiagram
    participant CS as Charging Station (Test System)
    participant CSMS as CSMS (System under Test)
    participant OCSP as OCSP Service (Test System)

    Note over CS,CSMS: Prerequisite: The configured eMAID is known by the CSMS as valid
    Note over CS,CSMS: Prerequisite: The contract certificate is revoked
    Note over CS,OCSP: Prerequisite: iso15118CertificateHashData has a responder URL<br>that points to an OCSP service for Test System
    Note over CS,CSMS: Prerequisite: CSMS does not have a cached OCSP response<br>for the contract certificate
    Note over CS,CSMS: Configuration State: N/a
    Note over CS,CSMS: Memory State: N/a
    Note over CS,CSMS: Execute Reusable State EVConnectedPreSession

    CS->>CSMS: AuthorizeRequest (idToken.idToken = Configured valid_idtoken_idtoken, idToken.type = Configured valid_idtoken_type, iso15118CertificateHashData = hashes from configured V2G certificate chain)

    CSMS->>OCSP: OCSP request to responder URL of iso15118CertificateHashData (check validity)
    Note over CSMS: Validation: CSMS sends an OCSP request<br>for iso15118CertificateHashData

    OCSP-->>CSMS: OCSP response (certificate is valid)
    Note over OCSP: Validation: Test System checks that received request<br>for iso15118CertificateHashData is valid
    Note over CSMS,OCSP: Remark: header step 3 says "valid", while the prerequisite<br>and the expected result in step 4 indicate a revoked certificate

    CSMS-->>CS: AuthorizeResponse (idTokenInfo.status = Invalid, certificateStatus = CertificateRevoked)
    Note over CSMS: Validation: AuthorizeResponse with<br>idTokenInfo.status Invalid<br>certificateStatus CertificateRevoked

    Note over CS,CSMS: Post scenario validation: EV is not authorized and shall not charge.<br>Charging Station does not send TransactionEventRequest with<br>triggerReason = Authorized or chargingState = Charging
